% microgpt2 block render: softmax with the visible stabilizing max-shift,
% m = BIG MAX (the genuine library big operator over the tape node), and
% the normalizer as a genuine Sigma over the tape -- SUM reopened for the
% autodiff node by the except-import route, so the denominator of
% softmax(z)_i = e^(z_i)/SUM_j e^(z_j) is the literature's own operator and
% not a named function standing in for it.  Z is bound rather than inlined:
% a reduction is a FlowExpr in the spec's grammar, so an inline division by
% one needs parentheses, and Z is both the partition function's own name and
% Karpathy's own structure (total = sum(exps)).  The signature states the
% paper's own membership, softmax : RR^n -> Delta^(n-1); the
% ProbDist(... .xs) lift is the whole price of saying it without a
% (spec-sanctioned, unimplemented) transparent type alias.
% From explorations/microgpt2.fss. Regenerate:
%   bin/fortick explorations/fortify/block-softmax.tic
%   TEXINPUTS=".:$FORTRESS_HOME/Fortify:" latex block-softmax.tex
%   dvisvgm --no-fonts --exact-bbox -o block-softmax-light.svg block-softmax.dvi
%   dark: add fill='#e6edf3' to the <svg> root tag
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{fortify}
\usepackage[active,tightpage]{preview}
\setlength\PreviewBorder{6pt}
\begin{document}
\begin{preview}
`softmax(a: Vec): ProbDist = do
  m = BIG MAX[u <- a] u
  e = exp(a - m)
  Z = SUM[u <- e] u
  ProbDist((e / Z).xs)
end`
\end{preview}
\end{document}
